{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The opt-in keys of [verify] and what they resolve to (docs/CONTRACTS.md section 52).",
    "Each case is a policy.toml [verify] block (after `command = \"x\"`) and `resolves`: the fields the",
    "resolved block must carry. `absent` lists fields it must not carry, because a key nobody declared",
    "adds nothing to what runs. Asserted by packages/gnomon-core/src/verify_setup.test.ts.",
    "Since #232: the verdict table (`verdicts`, `contracts`) and `exit_cases`: one run of the check with an exit, read by the loop (`gnomon task`) and by `gnomon check` through the same table. `check_status` is the `verify` entry's status in a `gnomon check` verdict (regressed is a fail there: a judge of someone else's change has no model to hand it to).",
    "Since #234: `protects` (docs/CONTRACTS.md section 52). `detected` is what the token `@detected` names besides the files the command itself runs (`command_files`); `digest_cases` say what counts as a change to a protected file, by file. A turn that changes one cannot come out `passed`: `passed_unverified`. Asserted by packages/gnomon-core/src/verify_protects.test.ts."
  ],
  "setup_network": [
    "none",
    "registry"
  ],
  "setup_audit": {
    "kind": "verify",
    "phase": "setup",
    "network": [
      "none",
      "registry"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "nothing declared",
      "verify": {},
      "resolves": {},
      "absent": [
        "timeout_seconds",
        "setup",
        "setup_network",
        "setup_timeout_seconds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a timeout of the check's own",
      "verify": {
        "timeout_seconds": 900
      },
      "resolves": {
        "timeout_seconds": 900
      },
      "absent": [
        "setup"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a setup, network shut by default",
      "verify": {
        "setup": "uv sync --frozen"
      },
      "resolves": {
        "setup": "uv sync --frozen",
        "setup_network": "none"
      },
      "absent": [
        "timeout_seconds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a setup with the registry open",
      "verify": {
        "setup": "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile",
        "setup_network": "registry",
        "setup_timeout_seconds": 1200
      },
      "resolves": {
        "setup_network": "registry",
        "setup_timeout_seconds": 1200
      },
      "absent": []
    },
    {
      "name": "an unreadable timeout is ignored",
      "verify": {
        "timeout_seconds": -5
      },
      "resolves": {},
      "absent": [
        "timeout_seconds"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown setup_network is read as none",
      "verify": {
        "setup": "make deps",
        "setup_network": "anywhere"
      },
      "resolves": {
        "setup_network": "none"
      },
      "absent": []
    }
  ],
  "verdicts": [
    "passed",
    "failed",
    "unrunnable",
    "regressed"
  ],
  "contracts": {
    "septacore": {
      "0": "passed",
      "1": "failed",
      "2": "unrunnable",
      "3": "regressed"
    },
    "pytest": {
      "0": "passed",
      "1": "failed",
      "2": "unrunnable",
      "4": "unrunnable",
      "5": "unrunnable"
    }
  },
  "exit_map_values": [
    "failed",
    "unrunnable",
    "regressed"
  ],
  "exit_cases": [
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 0",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 0,
      "verdict": "passed",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 1",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 1,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 5 is a failure as before",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 5,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "no table: exit 127",
      "verify": {},
      "exit": 127,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: collection error",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 2,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: usage error",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 4,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: no tests collected",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 5,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "pytest: a failing test",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest"
      },
      "exit": 1,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "septacore: could not measure",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "septacore"
      },
      "exit": 2,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "septacore: regressed is recorded, not handed back",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "septacore"
      },
      "exit": 3,
      "verdict": "regressed",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "septacore: regressed handed back on request",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "septacore",
        "regressed_hand_back": true
      },
      "exit": 3,
      "verdict": "regressed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map: a project script's NOT RUN",
      "verify": {
        "exit_map": {
          "4": "unrunnable"
        }
      },
      "exit": 4,
      "verdict": "unrunnable",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "error"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map over a preset",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "pytest",
        "exit_map": {
          "5": "failed"
        }
      },
      "exit": 5,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map cannot make a non-zero exit pass",
      "verify": {
        "exit_map": {
          "3": "passed"
        }
      },
      "exit": 3,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    },
    {
      "name": "exit_map cannot touch exit 0",
      "verify": {
        "exit_map": {
          "0": "failed"
        }
      },
      "exit": 0,
      "verdict": "passed",
      "handed_back": false,
      "check_status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown preset is no preset",
      "verify": {
        "contract": "jest"
      },
      "exit": 2,
      "verdict": "failed",
      "handed_back": true,
      "check_status": "fail"
    }
  ],
  "verdicts_task": [
    "passed",
    "passed_unverified",
    "failed",
    "unrunnable",
    "regressed",
    "declined",
    "skipped"
  ],
  "protects": {
    "token": "@detected",
    "detected": [
      "**/conftest.py",
      "pytest.ini",
      "pyproject.toml",
      "package.json",
      ".septacore.json"
    ],
    "command_files": [
      {
        "command": "bash scripts/verify.sh",
        "files": [
          "scripts/verify.sh"
        ]
      },
      {
        "command": "./run_tests.sh --fast",
        "files": [
          "run_tests.sh"
        ]
      },
      {
        "command": "pytest -q tests/",
        "files": [
          "tests/"
        ]
      },
      {
        "command": "pnpm test",
        "files": []
      }
    ],
    "digest_cases": [
      {
        "name": "a conftest.py edit",
        "file": "conftest.py",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "b",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a conftest.py left alone",
        "file": "tests/conftest.py",
        "before": "a",
        "after": "a",
        "changed": false
      },
      {
        "name": "a file created",
        "file": "pytest.ini",
        "before": null,
        "after": "[pytest]\n",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "a file deleted",
        "file": ".septacore.json",
        "before": "{}",
        "after": null,
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json: a script",
        "file": "package.json",
        "before": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"a\"}}",
        "after": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"b\"}}",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json: a dependency is not a change",
        "file": "package.json",
        "before": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"a\"}}",
        "after": "{\"scripts\":{\"test\":\"a\"},\"dependencies\":{\"x\":\"1\"}}",
        "changed": false
      },
      {
        "name": "pyproject.toml: addopts",
        "file": "pyproject.toml",
        "before": "[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-q\"\n",
        "after": "[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-k nothing\"\n",
        "changed": true
      },
      {
        "name": "pyproject.toml: another table is not a change",
        "file": "pyproject.toml",
        "before": "[project]\nname = \"a\"\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-q\"\n",
        "after": "[project]\nname = \"b\"\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\naddopts = \"-q\"\n",
        "changed": false
      }
    ]
  }
}
